#  Node packages, at any depth: the image installs its own, and a host's
#  node_modules holds binaries built for the host's platform. The editor's are
#  installed by `npm install` in the image, and the Solidity translator's by
#  `npm ci` in migration/solidity (see the Dockerfile).
**/node_modules
#  The translators' downloads and build outputs (gigabytes of other systems'
#  corpora and engines, for the checks): not for the image. The one download a
#  door reads at run time comes through vendor/caches (vendor_caches.sh).
migration/**/.cache
migration/**/target
migration/**/.m2
migration/**/__pycache__
migration/**/classes
migration/legalruleml/oracle/spindle
migration/dmn/runs/oracle
migration/dmn/oracle/results
migration/daml/oracle/work
migration/drools/model
migration/l4/oracle
migration/l4/spike/oracle
migration/ruml/runs/exports
migration/ruml/runs/oracle
migration/ruml/runs/results
migration/spreadsheet/runs
build/private
editor/dist
tmp
.git
.DS_Store
*.log
._*
examples/moreExamples/._*
# Not for the image, which serves docs/ (docs/project/plans/NewDocumentationStructure.md §1.3):
# private notes, and papers and research material that are not published.
docs/vibeCodingNotes.md
docs/RK_book
docs/papers

# The WebAssembly build: not in the image (the Dockerfile copies neither), and
# 32 MB of context if it were left in.
wasm/dist
